<item>
  <title>An interactive transport profile</title>
  <dc:creator>James Hulse</dc:creator>
  <link>https://hulsiejames.github.io/articles/interactive-network-demo/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<div class="vignette-summary">
<p><strong>This is a demonstration, not a real dataset.</strong> It shows the kind of interactive, well-documented analysis this site can host: a question, an explicit method, an explorable result and enough source to reproduce it.</p>
</div>
<section id="the-question" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="the-question">The question</h2>
<p>How does the shape of a daily travel profile change by mode, and what happens when the morning peak becomes more pronounced?</p>
<p>The chart below is generated in the reader’s browser with Observable JS. It needs no server and works on a static GitHub Pages site.</p>
</section>
